$DIR/test.p:14:11: cannot use &S{} (value of type *S) as I value in variable declaration: *S does not implement I (method Id has type parameters, so it cannot implement an interface method)
		have Id[U any]() int
		want Id() int
    _ is declared as I, so it can only hold values of that type; &S{} is a *S.
    Plutonium, like Go, does not convert between different types automatically.
    (see "Interface types" in the Plutonium spec, section 7.9)
    (run "pluto explain E0021" for a longer explanation)
